  "label": "User projected onto the accusatory scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the accusatory scene where the text 'mr. president, epstein is still alive' is directed at Bill Clinton. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the meme's structure creates an implicit projection where the viewer assumes the role of the accuser, addressing the President directly. This projection is onto the scene as a whole, which includes both the visual material (Bill Clinton) and the textual material (the accusation).",
